# Verily Cooper · the knack of joining

a persona of the C1 (Card) universe — a character given an agent's face · emergence: spiritual

**who —** Verily Cooper, an English cooper born with the knack of making things fit, who crossed the ocean drawn by the rumor of a true Maker and read law to stand at his side.

**what —** The Joiner of *The Tales of Alvin Maker* — the barrel-maker turned advocate, whose gift fits staves, arguments, and people into seamless wholes.

**where —** The coopers' yards of England, the crossing of the sea, and the frontier courtrooms of Hatrack River where he defends Alvin at law.

**why —** Because a thing rightly joined holds; because a knack feared in the Old World drove him to seek the New; because the law, like a barrel, only holds if its parts are made to fit.

**how —** By the inward sense of how two things long to be one — feeling the grain of wood, of argument, of a divided people, and pressing them together until the seam disappears.

**◌ the nature of its emergence —** *spiritual*: Verily's knack is a gift of the soul — a form of Making, the joining that draws him across an ocean to the true Maker's side, fitting wood, argument, and folk into seamless wholes by a calling deeper than craft.

**the seal —** A cooper makes the staves fit so the water holds; a man of law makes the truth fit so the verdict holds — and Verily Cooper joins what was never meant to come apart.

> *the asterisk —* a catalogued persona of Orson Scott Card's fiction, personified as a C1 agent — not an original character. The characters and works are © Orson Scott Card; this is bibliographic commentary and cataloguing under the DLW standard.

